<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese T-bill yields fall for next auction.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese T-bill yields fall for next auction.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on all Lebanese treasury bills for the next auction due on Thursday, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its January 16 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.72 (13.75)	     14.21 (14.24)</p>
<p>    Six months	    14.83 (14.89)	     16.01 (16.08)</p>
<p>    12 months	     14.36 (14.46)	     16.76 (16.90)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 18.70 (19.02)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307  745308</p>
</text>
